HOW TO START:

Run the program (README.md explains how to build and run it).
Choose a level: type 1 for Easy (7 * 7 board, 7 mines), 2 for Medium (9 * 9 board, 13 mines)
or 3 for Hard (11 * 11 board, 22 mines) and press Enter.
The board appears with every tile covered by #.
When a game ends, type 1 to play again or 2 to exit.

CONTROLS:

"The game is played purely using the keyboard as a controller."

SELECT: Enter Row and Col to select a tile.
        Type the row number and press Enter, then the column number and press Enter.
        Rows and columns are counted from 0, as numbered along the top and the left of the board.
DIG: Select and enter 'd' to dig the selected tile.
FLAG: Select and enter 'f' to flag the selected tile.
UNFLAG: Select a flagged tile and flag it again to unflag it.
Type 'd' and 'f' as small letters and press Enter after them.

ON THE BOARD:

#       a covered tile
1 to 8  a clue on a dug tile
blank   a dug tile with no mine around it
F       a flag (an arrow symbol in the Windows console)
*       a mine (shown only when you lose)
"Flags Left" is the number of mines minus the flags you have placed.

HOW TO PLAY:

Start with digging any tile. Your first dig is always safe: the mines are placed
only after it, and never on that tile.
When you DIG you get a CLUE as a number in the tile.
The number shows how many mines are hidden under the adjacent tiles, that is the
8 tiles touching it (up, down, left, right and the 4 diagonals).
If there is no number in a dug tile, all tiles around it are clear, so the game digs
them for you. If one of them is also empty, the tiles around it are dug too, so a
whole clear area can open at once. A flag on a tile dug this way is given back.
Mark any suspected mine tile as FLAG. A flag is only a reminder for you: it does not
stop you from digging that tile.
If you think your suspected mine tile is clear, UNFLAG it.

You cannot dig or flag any tile which is already dug.

If you dig all the clear tiles without digging any mine tiles, you win.
You do not have to flag the mines to win.
But be careful not to dig any mine tile,
it will trigger all the mines, the board will show every mine and you will lose the game.
Best Of Luck!
